49,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192742#post1192742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do Heralds do?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Herald is the high priest of the Beast's cult (or manager, if it's secular). They act as the spiritual go-between for the Beast's Horror and her human cultists, and defend the Begotten's Life while also perpetuating her Legend. From a mechanics point of view, they're like Primordial Dream Stigmatics. They also, from a narrative point of view, act in the role of the monster's second in command/trusted lieutenant/scheming general. Like many examples of those characters, they sometimes get different ideas about who should be in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 03-07-2018, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T13:55:07-08:00","id":1192751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192742#post1192742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do Heralds do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heralds are to Beasts as Sadikh are to Mummies. They get a different suite of powers since the source is dramatically different, but they have similar niches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:11:23-08:00","id":1192756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192749#post1192749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Herald is the high priest of the Beast's cult (or manager, if it's secular). They act as the spiritual go-between for the Beast's Horror and her human cultists, and defend the Begotten's Life while also perpetuating her Legend. From a mechanics point of view, they're like Primordial Dream Stigmatics. They also, from a narrative point of view, act in the role of the monster's second in command/trusted lieutenant/scheming general. Like many examples of those characters, they sometimes they get different ideas about who should be in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they are The Dragon to the Beast's Big Bad. I've been reading it on my phone and I've only been able to do the lightest of skims, but this looks GOOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:11:32-08:00","id":1192757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192735#post1192735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really happy Heralds and cults made it in. This gives Beast a lot more options in terms of stories to tell.<br /> <br /> Also, I really want to see a writeup for the Lodge of the Red Owl in the Contagion Chronicle. An Iron Master lodge with a Beast as a totem! That's awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a writer on the Contagion Chronicle, but I <i>do </i>have some Mystery Cult Initiation mechanics for all the little sample cults that are mentioned in that section, which I will post soon with some other cut/extra Cult material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:13:45-08:00","id":1192759,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I was uneasy about the Player Guide, but a friend who got the book has been sharing snippets of the writing, and it sounds like it's <i>much</i> more conscious of the harmfulness of Beasts and of showing characters and factions (!) who are constructive and grappling with their inherent moral difficulties.<br /> <br /> I mean, I expected it to be, knowing people were working hard on it to make it a worthwhile, redeeming, supplement, but it's an immense relief to <i>know </i>those perspectives are integral to the Player Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:26:58-08:00","id":1192772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192757#post1192757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a writer on the Contagion Chronicle, but I <i>do </i>have some Mystery Cult Initiation mechanics for all the little sample cults that are mentioned in that section, which I will post soon with some other cut/extra Cult material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay!<br /> <br /> Kinship merits are an awesome idea! Its neat to have a way to pick of some of the characteristics of other splats if you are trying to emulate a specific type of monster. Scour Your Body is a particularly interesting and non-obvious one for Mage. <br /> <br /> Legendary Horror is also AWESOME! Ways to get access to Influences are always fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:36:39-08:00","id":1192814,"title":"","content":"Before I pick up the pdf, what are the new Families and Hungers like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:45:04-08:00","id":1192821,"title":"","content":"I've done little more than skim so far, but even just a glance at the table of contents and a few inside pages tell me this is likely to be my favorite <i>CofD</i> book. The wealth of material here should do a lot to flesh out the world of Beast as one that can stand on its own, as well as giving even more rich opportunities for crossovers and fun plots!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192759#post1192759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I expected it to be, knowing people were working hard on it to make it a worthwhile, redeeming, supplement, but it's an immense relief to <i>know </i>those perspectives are integral to the Player Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I personally don't really think <i>Beast </i>needed &quot;redeeming,&quot; I do find this reaction nice, and hope that the quality of the Player's Guide might go a long way to changing some skeptics' minds about the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","user":"Gellydog","date":". 03-07-2018, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:57:10-08:00","id":1192830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192759#post1192759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit I was uneasy about the Player Guide, but a friend who got the book has been sharing snippets of the writing, and it sounds like it's <i>much</i> more conscious of the harmfulness of Beasts and of showing characters and factions (!) who are constructive and grappling with their inherent moral difficulties.<br /> <br /> I mean, I expected it to be, knowing people were working hard on it to make it a worthwhile, redeeming, supplement, but it's an immense relief to <i>know </i>those perspectives are integral to the Player Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192821#post1192821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I personally don't really think <i>Beast </i>needed &quot;redeeming,&quot; I do find this reaction nice, and hope that the quality of the Player's Guide might go a long way to changing some skeptics' minds about the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which for starters:<br /> <br /> In the opening fiction, we see some very conflicted Begotten.<br /> <br /> Two of them are middle school kids, and while both of them recognize their Horrors' Hunger to destroy and to hurt others, they themselves realize that this is wrong and not something they enjoy doing. The other two are adults, and similarly also consider when it's not ok to indulge in their Hungers, and at least stop to consider the consequences of what would happen afterwards if they indulged in their Hunger.<br /> <br /> So in other words...no, Beasts are not unaware sociopathic sadists who enjoy causing pains to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T20:34:57-08:00","id":1192946,"title":"","content":"The opening fiction is certainly very interesting; we've seen bits of it before, which was unexpected. There's a continuation of another story, a recontextualization of one of the first pieces of Beast writing to be revealed, and a reference to a Changeling story. That's neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T20:37:16-08:00","id":1192947,"title":"","content":"I'm deep into Chapter 2 right now, the subsection on Hunger/feeding...anyone else find this bit freakin' hilarious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T21:22:13-08:00","id":1192955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm most interested in what the two new Families are like.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192814#post1192814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I pick up the pdf, what are the new Families and Hungers like?</div> </div> </div> </div>WELL.<br /> <br /> (as a heads up, this is my impressions from the splat write-ups only and not the expanded &quot;how to play [Family/Hunger]&quot; section before it)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Families</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Inguma: Nightmares of the Other </b><br /> <br /> Called as the youngest Family, the Outsiders preys on the fears of the people who don't fit in. Who are anyone who don't fit the cultural norm of a community. This Beast could be someone who deliberately disregards common dress or custom, or the guy that does, on the surface, fit into the community, until people realize that no one knows who this guy is. Some of the cultural monsters that belong to this family include the Haitian M\u00e8tminwi, the Japanese noppera-bo, and the Albanian Catalan.<br /> <br /> So yeah, pretty straight-forward all considering. Fear of Other is an easily understandable and relatable fear that one could do a lot with. I can picture depicting them as Lovecraft horrors like Deep Ones or even modern stuff like Slenderman...but not much else.<br /> <br /> One major criticism from me is the Lives section and how...odd the different Begotten write-ups are in it:<ul><li>The first one with the flight attendant and the way her thing is described (reminding the passengers of a plane that she might be &quot;the last person I ever see on the ground&quot;), I have no idea how it connects to &quot;fear of the other&quot;.</li> <li>The second write-up involves a homeless man, panning for change. And it has the specific mention of &quot;tech hipsters&quot; avoiding the homeless man and avoid tipping him, because they fear of how &quot;one bad business decision could turn them into him&quot;...but then go on to say that the bankers flip him a coin for good luck before their big meeting. I'm...not sure what this write-up is trying to say.</li> <li>The third one is the most uncomfortable: it's about a guy that's been watching/stalking a woman who he deduces has been stood-up by a date. That the guy is contemplating swooping him to charm her, that he'll: &quot;throw in a few attraction spikes, initiate kino a couple times, and she\u2019ll be thinking of him all night. Whether she wants to or not.&quot; Uh...yeaaaahhh...even then, still have no idea what this does on relating back to &quot;Fear of the Other&quot;. Also, I have no idea what PUA training, or &quot;initiate kino&quot; is.</li> <li>The fourth involves a consultant to a company giving a presentation. And how her presentation involves...cutting down on the number of employees in the HR department.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So...yeah. Lives section leaves me confused. Rest of the write-up is fine though.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I believe a while ago, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> expressed a concern about the Inguma write-up getting into uncomfortable territory of having fear of the Other be equivalent to fear of oppressed minorities...no, the splat write-up avoids calling attention to any specific demographic. The only thing that comes remotely close is the mention of a woman clutching her purse and having to walk through the &quot;bad&quot; part of town...but that's about it. It does not call attention to specific racial or ethnic demographic. And, well, broadly speaking, most major urban areas in any part of the world has at least *a* bad part of town. So just mentioning it doesn't really raise any red flags, at least to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Talassii: Nightmares of Confinement</b><br /> <br /> The Captors are hinted at being the rarest and also the most misunderstood by the other Families. Mostly due to an unfortunate stigma left from a Hero labeling them as kidnappers and rapists. Something that the Captors have been working against all these years later, retraining themselves from ever laying a hand on their prey and indulging in any unnecessarily cruel and unusual punishments. That it's all about capturing and holding their targets, and depriving them of their home and safe place. Cultural monsters for this Family include the Central African eloko, the Slavic leshy, and the Brazilian encantado.<br /> <br /> When I first heard about this Family I was...initially kind of confused. I thought that &quot;Confinement&quot; seemed like an overly specific and niche type of fear. The kind that really didn't provide enough plot and story hooks to work with and was a paper-thin character concept.<br /> <br /> Of course, my mind was changed when I actually read the splat write-up.<br /> <br /> The write-up frames it as being the loss of freedom and control. Of taking away the familiar and comforting environment of the prey and having them deal with the new and unfamiliar surroundings to them. So...yeah, that sold the Family to me, and opens a lot more story hooks then I initially thought.<br /> <br /> Gonna save a different post for Hungers, since this one is getting long already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:11:36-08:00","id":1193019,"title":"","content":"The two Hungers are Secrets and Transgression and they are amoral rather than immoral. Secrets can be downright heroic as you get your thrill from knowing the things not keeping it under wraps.<br /> <br /> Transgression can be played as the Hebrew devil splat but an interesting thing is that transgression is noted to be relative. Persuading a cult member to renunce their sect or a Centimani to return to the Pilgrimnage should be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:47:11-08:00","id":1193069,"title":"","content":"Are the Heralds, cults and Horrorspawn any fun? Or are they too cumbersome to use in regular play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:22:51-08:00","id":1193100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193069#post1193069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Heralds, cults and Horrorspawn any fun? Or are they too cumbersome to use in regular play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, they're pretty awesome. A Cult is mechanically just a Staff with a specialized function and some potential extra Merits (and risk of becoming Heroes if you abuse them), a Herald is a guy with some Beast abilities who is completely playable. Horrorspawn are more complex, but if you can make a Horror using the notebook, you can make them; only real bookkeeping is keeping track of the Satiety investment and preventing the Horror from reabsorbing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:44:56-08:00","id":1193147,"title":"","content":"This book is giving me life hadn't been enjoying a RPG book like this in a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:21:40-08:00","id":1193217,"title":"","content":"Love the book! the Opening fiction has a character named Vince who I very much enjoyed. He can sense the Beasts and their rising hungers and Horrors, but has no Horror, and I'm pretty sure he laid an Anathama on the Lurker that was going after the kids, making me think he is a Hero, but his actions suggest that he has no enmity toward the children Beasts and actively tries to protect them and help them. Would he be the hinted at form of friendly, sane Dreamer-Hero that manages to hold true to his Integrity much like the original Dreamers of ancient days that were in touch with the Primordial Dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 03-08-2018, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:30:04-08:00","id":1193256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192749#post1192749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They act as the spiritual go-between for the Beast's Horror and her human cultists</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting bit. I could see a Herald playing an intersting role in any conflict between a Beast's human drives and her Horror's.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:37:54-08:00","id":1193262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193256#post1193256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very interesting bit. I could see a Herald playing an intersting role in any conflict between a Beast's human drives and her Horror's.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you just need a friend to tell you you're being an asshole. Beasts can be pretty big assholes, so they need pretty good friends.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:29:11-08:00","id":1193287,"title":"","content":"Do you think the Inguma do a good job embodiying fear of BEING Othered and disconnected, or would the Gorgons fit better there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:36:29-08:00","id":1193292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193287#post1193287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the Inguma do a good job embodiying fear of BEING Othered and disconnected, or would the Gorgons fit better there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Namtaru are good for the 'Other to be reviled/unclean one', whereas the Inguma do the 'Other that infiltrates your life and corrupts it' very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:58:35-08:00","id":1193320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193019#post1193019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two Hungers are Secrets and Transgression and they are amoral rather than immoral. Secrets can be downright heroic as you get your thrill from knowing the things not keeping it under wraps.<br /> <br /> Transgression can be played as the Hebrew devil splat but an interesting thing is that transgression is noted to be relative. Persuading a cult member to renunce their sect or a Centimani to return to the Pilgrimnage should be possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go into further detail:<br /> <br /> The Whispers (those that Hunger for Secrets) are also described as being the most crossover friendly...both for and against the other splats. Obviously on cozying up to the other secret-seeking splats: the Carthian Mekhet, the Darkling Autumn Courtier, the Obrimos from the Mysterium, etc. It's also noted that the Whispers are the ones that most commonly hunt Kin.<br /> <br /> The Enablers (those that Hunger for Transgressions) are perhaps the most equipped for dealing with Heroes...in the sense that they are the ones that could convince one that their Quest is bullshit. That they need to let go of their Heroic pursuit, that their &quot;code&quot; is not worth fighting for.<br /> <br /> ...and, well, in general, for those that criticized the final draft for crowbarring in Lessons on top of the existing core Hungers, these two new ones are better and cleaner fits to explore Lessons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:42:30-08:00","id":1193335,"title":"","content":"Skimming through the sections that most jumped out at me and so far none have disappointed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I see that there is a secondary running theme in the player's guide beyond &quot;No Neat Boxes&quot;, (which is freak'n amazing by the way. This concept of flexible mechanics and lore to explore is one of my favorite aspects of the Chronicles of Darkness.) The Players Guide focuses on the &quot;Internal Conflicts&quot; that make Beast such a fascinating game. From rich details about how to approach the Gestalt/Symbiotic relationship between the Beast and their Horror, to further examinations of how the individual mechanics narratively effect the Begotten, to detailing political and religious aspects of the Begotten community, and of course those lovely new Inheritance mechanics. This opens so many new doors to explore with Beast, and I cannot thank the developers enough for such a loving examination of the gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:45:53-08:00","id":1193337,"title":"","content":"Well, the Four Pathes could give Beasts some interesting resonance with Prometheans. Incarnation is a very different destination than the Pilgramage, but it's a journey all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:59:39-08:00","id":1193343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193320#post1193320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...and, well, in general, for those that criticized the final draft for crowbarring in Lessons on top of the existing core Hungers, these two new ones are better and cleaner fits to explore Lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was very much at the forefront of my brain when I did the write-ups and expansion sections for the new Hungers. I think the lesson thing works fine in the core <i>conceptually</i>, but because of the last-minute nature of the changes, it often isn't supported by the unaltered text. It's probably an understatement to say that <b>Beast </b>has a bit of a text vs. subtext problem, but I'll cop to contributing to that problem, so it is what it is.<br /> <br /> I made sure the Whispers and Enablers had a lot of textual support for the idea that they could credibly teach lessons, and that they can be more than just abuse-machines...at least within the shaky morality of using fear to make a point (cf., &quot;Beasts are assholes&quot;). Enablers in particular, who I hope come off as more than just hedonism machines. There's a reason they can't just, like, spike vegan meals with meat and cackle evilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:26:17-08:00","id":1193350,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not through the whole book yet (I'm actually reading this one cover-to-cover, instead of skipping around like I usually do), but I've tried to find this and haven't had much luck.<br /> <br /> Is there anyway that gives a specific description to the Anathema the Talassii family is under? At times the text just seems to imply it was just a figurative hit to their reputation, but other places seem to indicate it's a full-on, mystical Anathema that can be &quot;broken&quot; somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T16:36:07-08:00","id":1193354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193350#post1193350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm not through the whole book yet (I'm actually reading this one cover-to-cover, instead of skipping around like I usually do), but I've tried to find this and haven't had much luck.<br /> <br /> Is there anyway that gives a specific description to the Anathema the Talassii family is under? At times the text just seems to imply it was just a figurative hit to their reputation, but other places seem to indicate it's a full-on, mystical Anathema that can be &amp;quot;broken&amp;quot; somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s really been frustrating me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T17:04:30-08:00","id":1193361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193350#post1193350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm not through the whole book yet (I'm actually reading this one cover-to-cover, instead of skipping around like I usually do), but I've tried to find this and haven't had much luck.<br /> <br /> Is there anyway that gives a specific description to the Anathema the Talassii family is under? At times the text just seems to imply it was just a figurative hit to their reputation, but other places seem to indicate it's a full-on, mystical Anathema that can be &quot;broken&quot; somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that their reputation is more or less completely tainted, and their Horrors always come off as menacing, no matter what they intend (that's in the Horror section on p. 48). It doesn't have a mechanical effect, it's more that (narratively) their credibility is mystically ruined. That would be my interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T17:26:26-08:00","id":1193367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193361#post1193361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that their reputation is more or less completely tainted, and their Horrors always come off as menacing, no matter what they intend (that's in the Horror section on p. 48). It doesn't have a mechanical effect, it's more that (narratively) their credibility is mystically ruined. That would be my interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! I thought it might be something like that, but I wasn't quite sure. It's definitely an interesting take, to have even other Beasts unable to shake the feeling that all Captors are creepy creepsters. I also have to believe that it's used as a subtle way of nudging players away from some of the more...unpleasant interpretations of &quot;Fear of Confinement.&quot; Giving the Talassii a canon collective aversion to rape and out-and-out physical torture certainly seems like a proactive attempt to head off some really gross Beast concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:00:51-08:00","id":1193373,"title":"","content":"I'm abit concerned about why two beasts mating in horror form was actually added to the game as the primary method to gain horrorspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:17:06-08:00","id":1193380,"title":"","content":"How does one bring out the minion or thrall lair trait out into the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:36:48-08:00","id":1193395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193373#post1193373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm abit concerned about why two beasts mating in horror form was actually added to the game as the primary method to gain horrorspawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it ties into the Dark Mother? It's no more uncomfortable than what the Circle of the Crone gets up to, and it's hardly the only way. It helps that it's explicitly a business transaction, and that it's mentioned that many Beasts are more comfortable with harvesting Spawn from dreams, because it is an expression of trust and somewhat uncomfortable for them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:41:39-08:00","id":1193397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193395#post1193395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it ties into the Dark Mother? It's no more uncomfortable than what the Circle of the Crone gets up to, and it's hardly the only way. It helps that it's explicitly a business transaction, and that it's mentioned that many Beasts are more comfortable with harvesting Spawn from dreams, because it is an expression of trust and somewhat uncomfortable for them too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is no where near enough justification IMO. It's thing like that which give WoD and CofD a bad reputation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:07:17-08:00","id":1193403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193373#post1193373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm abit concerned about why two beasts mating in horror form was actually added to the game as the primary method to gain horrorspawn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? Beast is a pretty visceral game, all about the blood and the meat and the screaming. Nothing is more visceral than physically mating. And it isn't the only method of creating a Horrorspawn if you don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:10:02-08:00","id":1193405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193397#post1193397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is no where near enough justification IMO. It's thing like that which give WoD and CofD a bad reputation.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a world where Vampire 2E exists and embraces sensuality, to the point of having a Merit for menses that generate supercharged blood for arcane rituals in the corebook, I fail to see how creating temporary minions that are explicitly extensions of yourself through consensual mind-sex treated as such is somehow verboten, either. Particularly given how this is the same book that introduces Enticers, aka playable succubi, and Talasii, who were named in-universe for the Rape of the Sabine Women after their ancestors tried to pull a similar stunt and were mightily smote for it. When you have two <i>character archetypes </i>that deal with sex, you've already gone into that territory; might as well have a positive example portrayed as an act of faith by two people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:27:46-08:00","id":1193409,"title":"","content":"Sex in the game is not an issue. Mechanics which incentivize &quot;Cthulhu x Dragon&quot; sex is my issue. This sort of stuff is why everyone tries to forget Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Also, Talasii is specifically not about sex. They're stereotyped as part of a curse and they make sure to not reinforce that image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-08-2018, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:41:17-08:00","id":1193412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193409#post1193409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex in the game is not an issue. Mechanics which incentivize &quot;Cthulhu x Dragon&quot; sex is my issue. This sort of stuff is why everyone tries to forget Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Also, Talasii is specifically not about sex. They're stereotyped as part of a curse and they make sure to not reinforce that image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Talasii are specifically not about rape. We're talking about consensual sex for the purpose of breeding, when indeed in mythology that's often where monsters come from (see Echidna &amp; Typhon, Loki &amp; Angreboda, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:42:18-08:00","id":1193413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193409#post1193409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex in the game is not an issue. Mechanics which incentivize &quot;Cthulhu x Dragon&quot; sex is my issue. This sort of stuff is why everyone tries to forget Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Also, Talasii is specifically not about sex. They're stereotyped as part of a curse and they make sure to not reinforce that image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stating a normal interaction that most living beings engage in as a possibility for reproduction is not 'incentivizing' sex of any kind. You are projecting your biases and finding issues where there are none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T20:54:36-08:00","id":1193416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193409#post1193409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex in the game is not an issue. Mechanics which incentivize &quot;Cthulhu x Dragon&quot; sex is my issue. This sort of stuff is why everyone tries to forget Changing Breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could conceivably range from nightmarish to poetic depending how it is conceptualized. I expect most tables would use a fade to black scene and not describe it. <br /> <br /> Butttttt... plunging into the stranger side of human appreciation of aesthetic, <a href=\"http://www.dailymotion.com/video/xdxbx\" target=\"_blank\">one of the BBC's most popular nature videos is this clip of slugs mating.</a> It's beautiful, emotional, and fascinating. All of those exist despite the fact that there is no sexualization and the sex is utterly alien to our own form of reproduction. <br /> <br /> When I read the bit about Beasts mating, I thought of this, I thought of people's dreams merging, and I thought of the creation of new life. That's all poinient stuff. If it's mediated through Cthulhu on Smaug action its odd, but not repulsive. If played right, there could even be a certain romance to it. It's certainly not even close to Werewolf 1e's murderous stillborn ghost-babies, which have thankfully been relegated to discontinuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-08-2018, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T21:03:48-08:00","id":1193418,"title":"","content":"Now I can say: I liked the opening fiction, and how it casts prior pieces of writing done for Beast differently. And overall? I think this book is actually rather good, and that brings me uncounted relief. I haven't gone through most of it properly yet, but it is without doubt much more conscientious and on point than the first book. For a few highlights, I really like the subchapter on the Primordial Dream and how Beasts relate to the rest of the Astral. The societies of Begotten, with their examples of starkly different attitudes on responsibility and purpose, are strong ideas and make me feel they really should have been in the corebook, in hindsight. Of the new stuff, I thought the Inguma, for being basically <i>the fear of other people, </i>were one of the most of the most interesting bits, but there are other things in the Player Guide worth the attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-09-2018, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T21:17:29-08:00","id":1193421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternal Darkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193413#post1193413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Stating a normal interaction that most living beings engage in as a possibility for reproduction is not 'incentivizing' sex of any kind. You are projecting your biases and finding issues where there are none.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh, I'm gonna have to side with Milo here; Horror Mating is explicitly and mechanically easier than harvesting a dream to make Horrorspawn eggs. You have a chance to fail the latter.<br /> <br /> It's not <i>much </i>of a chance, but it is distinctly easier, and Horrorspawn aren't really children, they're avatars of the Horror that will one day die or be reabsorbed. <br /> <br /> Still, though, I thought the problem with Changing Breeds was that it was poorly written, not the ties to sex. Sex just tends to stick out, because, well, it's sex. There's a whole social nexus of rules and acceptable behavior for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T21:17:32-08:00","id":1193422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193397#post1193397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is no where near enough justification IMO. It's thing like that which give WoD and CofD a bad reputation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that this Horror Spawn option is frankly rather tame if you're grouping WoD into this. Typhon and Echidna are the literal father and mother of monsters in Greek Mythology, and they didn't spawn legions without making the Beast with Two Backs. <br /> <br /> Plus...come on, the Tzimisce exist in WoD...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:04:51-08:00","id":1193432,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds problem was definitely not sex, and was definitely more that it was a very...<i>immature</i><i>ly</i> written supplement.<br /> <br /> I thought that sex was the main way to make Horrorspawn was kind of awesome, particularly since it didn't seem to care about gender for it, provided an asexual mean of production, and tied into a strong mythological and human core while also creating the means for minions. A Horde of Mini-Me's, nonetheless!<br /> <br /> It has a range of depth and meaning, is what I'm getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:17:30-08:00","id":1193436,"title":"","content":"Something I really liked about using sex to make Horrorspawn was it was <i>not</i> a natural ability the Horrors have. They are asexual, and totally lack things like chromosomes or (in most cases, probably) genitals...a.k.a. the things you need for sexual reproduction. The Horrors can only perform this function because they are connected <i>to a human</i>, for which this is totally natural.<br /> <br /> In other words, <i>the Horror is gaining superpowers by merging with a human being.</i><br /> <br /> It's a total inversion of the usual line that happens in not just the <i>CofD</i>, but most speculative fiction. In this case, <i>we're </i>alien being with bizarre, unnatural (to a Horror) powers that the Horror can only access because of the bond. We get Atavisms and Lairs, they get Merit: The Monster with Two Backs.<br /> <br /> And I, uh, think that's pretty neat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:21:32-08:00","id":1193437,"title":"","content":"Has there been anything said in this about the Homecoming at all, or is that still dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:24:46-08:00","id":1193438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193437#post1193437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been anything said in this about the Homecoming at all, or is that still dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devouring is well and fully the final form of it, but name asides, it's clear it has all the same deep connotation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:31:44-08:00","id":1193440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193437#post1193437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been anything said in this about the Homecoming at all, or is that still dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of.<br /> <br /> In the first chapter that expands on the Devouring, which is mostly about how varied a potential-Beast's varied reactions to it. One of them being, in a very Homecoming-way, about how some Beast candidates go through their entire life feeling that something makes them different from others but they aren't sure what. That when the Nightmares start happening, and the finally confront the Horror at the other end and learn what's what, that they feel relieved at the revelation. Reassured and confident that this is who they were meant to be, and accept the Devouring with open arms.<br /> <br /> Granted, it's not called the &quot;Homecoming&quot; anymore, and the major aspect of the Horror Devouring the human soul and replacing it with their's is still intact, but it at least provides an in-canon option to make a Devouring more like the old Homecoming if one prefers.<br /> <br /> (although it's not to the point of actually having different sub-categories of the Devouring or any mechanical benefits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:48:30-08:00","id":1193446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193436#post1193436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I really liked about using sex to make Horrorspawn was it was <i>not</i> a natural ability the Horrors have. They are asexual, and totally lack things like chromosomes or (in most cases, probably) genitals...a.k.a. the things you need for sexual reproduction. The Horrors can only perform this function because they are connected <i>to a human</i>, for which this is totally natural.<br /> <br /> In other words, <i>the Horror is gaining superpowers by merging with a human being.</i><br /> <br /> It's a total inversion of the usual line that happens in not just the <i>CofD</i>, but most speculative fiction. In this case, <i>we're </i>alien being with bizarre, unnatural (to a Horror) powers that the Horror can only access because of the bond. We get Atavisms and Lairs, they get Merit: The Monster with Two Backs.<br /> <br /> And I, uh, think that's pretty neat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I note that Horror reproduction does not necessarily have to be tab-A-slot-B. I mean, what if one Horror is an AI-like thing and another is a dragon? Perhaps their 'sex' could be more a 'meeting of minds', ala Athena's birth. Some of the methods of reproduction that first circle demons from Exalted employ spring to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:36:58-08:00","id":1193645,"title":"","content":"oh. hey. I just noticed that Dreamborn (which just are Goatia) are specifically called out to have the twilight form manifestation. I suppose we can put that to bed then. <br /> <br /> Also lesser thing i noticed that interested me, examples of beasts working with heros and sympathetic attention were given a good amount of secondary attention, and in turn it specifically called out Heroes cant from kinships, so that's neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:10:23-08:00","id":1193667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193416#post1193416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly not even close to Werewolf 1e's murderous stillborn ghost-babies, which have thankfully been relegated to discontinuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely hated that about Forsaken 1e. It took the isolation angle a bit too far, and utterly murdered a lot of potential inter-character plots by making packs into people who absolutely must not get TOO close while simultaneously expecting them to be closer than lovers in a way. It was such a weird disconnect for me and made absolutely no sense. I know it was done to enforce the idea that Uratha need to stay close to their human sides (i.e. human family) and because Apocalypse did it too, but as a person who is naturally Polyamorous and prefers very character-driven stories i utterly hated it to the point that it actually drove me away from ever touching Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193436#post1193436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I really liked about using sex to make Horrorspawn was it was <i>not</i> a natural ability the Horrors have. They are asexual, and totally lack things like chromosomes or (in most cases, probably) genitals...a.k.a. the things you need for sexual reproduction. The Horrors can only perform this function because they are connected <i>to a human</i>, for which this is totally natural.<br /> <br /> In other words, <i>the Horror is gaining superpowers by merging with a human being.</i><br /> <br /> It's a total inversion of the usual line that happens in not just the <i>CofD</i>, but most speculative fiction. In this case, <i>we're </i>alien being with bizarre, unnatural (to a Horror) powers that the Horror can only access because of the bond. We get Atavisms and Lairs, they get Merit: The Monster with Two Backs.<br /> <br /> And I, uh, think that's pretty neat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved this part, too. It really highlights how Horrors are otherworldy beings of nightmare, as malleable as dreams and also shows where they gain from their symbiotic relationship with humans in a very clear way, even beyond gaining access to a partner (the Beast) who can wield Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 03-09-2018, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:19:45-08:00","id":1193670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193380#post1193380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one bring out the minion or thrall lair trait out into the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get a physical vessel, either a person, animal, or part of the Beast's human body (which causes a little Aggravated damage). Tell the spawn to inhabit it. Profit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Da