ry/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193829#post1193829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please send me a link!</div> </div> </div> </div>I will when it's done. It may take a little while, as I'll have to fit it in around my main fic, Samyaza, and, you know, actual work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T23:55:59-08:00","id":1193831,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm having trouble with, though, is settling on a Horror and Hunger for Taylor, as well as deciding between Inguma and Makara for Family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T00:25:45-08:00","id":1193836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193820#post1193820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;While they can do no damage to intruders, minions can attempt to apply the Knocked Down, Stunned, or Immobilized Tilts.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> This seems to be the most useful thing to get out of the trait in the outside world, so I'd probably say that, like other Traits, when you impose it the Minions/Thralls sort of appear out of nothing (or through some suitably theatrical means, i.e. rising out of ground or clawing in through the walls) and can start interacting with that area as if it was part of the Lair. So, if you're trying to impose those listed Tilts they begin grabbing at the enemy, or maybe they can start messing with the scenery. The rest of the trait description mentions &amp;quot;maintaining or breaking down Chambers,&amp;quot; so maybe you could have them start breaking stuff or even build things up (like a bridge from nearby materials).<br /> <br /> Thralls can actually engage in combat and use one Atavism each, so you would just &amp;quot;summon&amp;quot; them into the scene and then order them around as you would in your Lair. At least, that's my interpretation!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok i do get how it's useful. But I'm failing to see the minions/Thralls resonance to bring it out. For let's say that's the only traits a beast has, what does he have to do to bring it out? Have real life lackies around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T00:29:13-08:00","id":1193837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193836#post1193836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok i do get how it's useful. But I'm failing to see the minions/Thralls resonance to bring it out. For let's say that's the only traits a beast has, what does he have to do to bring it out? Have real life lackies around?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would be restricted into only being able to open Primordial Pathways to your Lair from your Chambers and other Gateways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T00:33:51-08:00","id":1193838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193837#post1193837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you would be restricted into only being able to open Primordial Pathways to your Lair from your Chambers and other Gateways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that you can use whatever other Lair Traits you have. So if you have, say, Undergrowth and Thralls, you can impose Undergrowth on a location, then bring in Thralls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T01:42:21-08:00","id":1193845,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">If you indeed only had access to Minions and Thralls, I suppose any small group of people doing your bidding and capable of causing similar tilts would count. I dunno, Staff maybe?</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T08:55:56-08:00","id":1193935,"title":"","content":"As a rule, I found the BPG an excellent, top-quality sourcebook, as important to the game as the corebook itself, in almost all its components. Some stuff may look rather more valid and useful than a few other items that look mostly useless or redundant, but this is only natural. The only material that I'm really unhappy about is the Satiety management guidelines that imply Gorged is the only optimal Satiety condition for a Beast to be in (I strongly disagree, IMO Starving is at least just as optimal in its own way) and the Talassii curse for its rapey implications.<br /> <br /> Not because I have any squeamishness objections to using rape in fiction, quite the contrary, IMO it has a valid place in appropriate circumstances for drama or as an erotic fantasy, but because I absolutely despise the prudish, PC meme that sex is a sacred thing that should only happen with romantic love in a perfect relationship and hence rape is a &quot;special kind of evil&quot;, worse than killing and more so any other non-sexual violence, abuse, or coercion. In my opinion, sex is an important but vanilla part of life that people can legitimately and gainfully indulge in for all kinds of non-romantic reasons in all kinds of less than ideal situations, from erotic pleasure with no strings attached to personal experimentation or gratification to a transactional exchange. Sexual abuse does not warrant any special status, it is just the equivalent of non-sexual assault, blackmail, harassment, or torture (as the case may be, according to circumstances) that just happens to involve sexual stuff, nothing more, nothing less, and should be treated no differently.<br /> <br /> From this PoV of mine, in Beast terms I find way distasteful, arbitrary, and hypocrite to burden a Family with a special mystical curse since the entrapment fear archetype that birthed them may have some rapey implications, when Beasts of all kinds and Families often do nightmarish things to victims for feeding that are just as bad as or worse than sexual violation. Just think what a typical Tyrant, Predator, or Ravager can do to victims if they don't really care about the consequences of their actions, all the way to murder or absolutely ruining lives, that Nemeses might easily stoop down to excruciating torture, and stuff. Hence I've decided to ignore the Talassii's 'curse' at my table as prudish/PC nonsense and surgically cut it away from the setting. Last but not least, I have my serious doubts a single Hero could or should be able to burden an entire Family with a lasting curse. That kind of event should at least involve the intervention of a godlike entity (say, that hypothetical uber-Hero should at least have been to Heroes what an Incarnate is to Beasts).<br /> <br /> And I cling to my notion that while Sated and moreso Ravenous and Slumbering are dangerous and unpleasant situations that should usually be avoided barring special circumstances, Starving and Gorged at least are equally advantageous and useful conditions for a Beast to be in, each in their own way (I have my own reasons to prefer Starving, but I can see the reasons to choose Gorged instead), at least this side of the Incarnation Inheritance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:41:52-08:00","id":1193946,"title":"","content":"The reason sexual abuse warrants such different treatment is the statistical odds that someone at the table has actually experienced it, and it\u2019s highest correlation to number of real life ptsd cases compared to the other evil acts you listed.<br /> <br /> Obviously comfort level and psychological safety of specific players should be considered no matter the trauma, but by landslide that is the issue most likely to come up; and at the same time one of the least likely to be disclosed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-10-2018, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:52:38-08:00","id":1193953,"title":"","content":"Holy cow just finished the section on the Obascus rites and those are AMAZING. Kudos to the writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:03:03-08:00","id":1193956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193831#post1193831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm having trouble with, though, is settling on a Horror and Hunger for Taylor, as well as deciding between Inguma and Makara for Family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Namtaru, surely? The Atavism for turning into a swarm of insects belongs to them, and controlling masses of insects is her canonical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:05:54-08:00","id":1193959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193956#post1193956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Namtaru, surely? The Atavism for turning into a swarm of insects belongs to them, and controlling masses of insects is her canonical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>But she, as a person, previously to her Trigger, wasn't the sort of person whose greatest fear was a swarm of bugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:11:32-08:00","id":1193964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193959#post1193959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But she, as a person, previously to her Trigger, wasn't the sort of person whose greatest fear was a swarm of bugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and one can pick up Unfavored Atavisms too with a bit more work. She can develop that power later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:55:17-08:00","id":1193979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193959#post1193959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But she, as a person, previously to her Trigger, wasn't the sort of person whose greatest fear was a swarm of bugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You greatest fear does not necessarily have anything to do with your eventual Horror, and especially not in that way. Nightmares of Powerlessness lead to Anakim, but there don't have to be any actual Giants involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:58:48-08:00","id":1193980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193946#post1193946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason sexual abuse warrants such different treatment is the statistical odds that someone at the table has actually experienced it, and it\u2019s highest correlation to number of real life ptsd cases compared to the other evil acts you listed.<br /> <br /> Obviously comfort level and psychological safety of specific players should be considered no matter the trauma, but by landslide that is the issue most likely to come up; and at the same time one of the least likely to be disclosed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as far as I'm concerned it is just common sense and civility to respect some boundaries at the gaming table, such as agreeing to keep certain events strictly offstage that certain players may be seriously uncomfortable with. This is just something even the &quot;\u00a3$%&amp; your snowflake feelings&quot; anti-PC me can naturally agree with. gaming should be a pleasant experience for everyone. I just wish to keep all ptsd experiences equal, regardless of their hypothetical different statistical frequence.<br /> <br /> At most, I'm going to expect anyone that is willing to play a game in a setting as brutal as the CofD/WoD and with characters bound to a predatory lifestyle such as vampires, beasts, or werewolves is also able to accept a certain serious degree of violence, abuse, and violation as necessary and inevitable in the story and setting, of the sexual and non-sexual kind (given the importance sex has for humans and since most supernaturals come from human stock), even if the table may agree to keep them offstage. E.g. In all likelihood a sizable portion of the hunting activities of Beasts and of the nightmares caused by unleashed Horrors are going to have some sexual implications, even if we do not focus on them or give them explicit coverage. It is the same reason a certain degree of visceral brutality is inherent in this game and needs to be expected, even if we put some limits to its graphic representation.<br /> <br /> But as far as I'm concerned, this is an altogether different matter. I just find the prudish/PC notion entirely unacceptable sex should have a sacred status and hence violations of bodily integrity or personal freedom that happen to involve sexual organs or erogeous zones should be treated any differently from all the other cases. Again, statistical variations make no meaningful difference in this context. Hence I find the Tallassii special 'rapist' curse an horrible idea. Or otherwise we should expect most other Families to carry their own kind of curses, such as Anakim having a 'bully' curse, the Namtaru having a 'abomination' curse, the Makara a 'maneater' curse, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T11:19:39-08:00","id":1193986,"title":"","content":"The only other thing I'm unhappy with in the BPG is the implication achievement of Inheritance is necessarily going to be an endgame for the character. Now, most kinds of Inheritance admittedly make the character unplayable in a Beast chronicle, either because they turn animalistic (Merger, Retreat in most cases) or they effectively regress into a Muggle (Divergence, Erasure). But I cannot see any valid reason why an Incarnate cannot stay a playable character indefinitedly in a suitably high-powered chronicle, more or less under the same terms one can play an Archmage or vampire elder PC (stuff we have entire sourcebooks about). Incarnate Inheritance is basically the same kind of playable, trascendental supernatural condition as Archmagedom, if with less phenomenal cosmic power and more viscerally physical superpowers. Inversion is also entirely playable in theory, even if practice I expect it is going to cut short the character's lifespan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T11:27:28-08:00","id":1193989,"title":"","content":"If you really, <i>really </i>think that fear of rape is something you want to explore through your game, <i>and </i>you have a Storyteller and other players who are willing <i>and </i>comfortable with that, then there's absolutely nothing stopping you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd prefer it if my RPG books didn't include a passage called, &quot;And here's how you play a rape monster!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T11:39:39-08:00","id":1193991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193989#post1193989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really, <i>really </i>think that fear of rape is something you want to explore through your game, <i>and </i>you have a Storyteller and other players who are willing <i>and </i>comfortable with that, then there's absolutely nothing stopping you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd prefer it if my RPG books didn't include a passage called, &amp;quot;And here's how you play a rape monster!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to second this. Perfectly stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T11:53:59-08:00","id":1193994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193986#post1193986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only other thing I'm unhappy with in the BPG is the implication achievement of Inheritance is necessarily going to be an endgame for the character. Now, most kinds of Inheritance admittedly make the character unplayable in a Beast chronicle, either because they turn animalistic (Merger, Retreat in most cases) or they effectively regress into a Muggle (Divergence, Erasure). But I cannot see any valid reason why an Incarnate cannot stay a playable character indefinitedly in a suitably high-powered chronicle, more or less under the same terms one can play an Archmage or vampire elder PC (stuff we have entire sourcebooks about). Incarnate Inheritance is basically the same kind of playable, trascendental supernatural condition as Archmagedom, if with less phenomenal cosmic power and more viscerally physical superpowers. Inversion is also entirely playable in theory, even if practice I expect it is going to cut short the character's lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not all Beasts want to or have to go for Inheritance (e.g. Predators are mentioned to quite often forego that option, as they often consider their 'normal' status to be the Dark Mother's will, 'pure', and a sort of perfect state/existence).<br /> Also, as you yourself pointed out, Archmages and Elder Vampire PCs became an option once we had Sourcebooks for them - this is not the case for Beasts, currently, but that could very well change at some point (Hell, I'm all for that!). In addition, I don't see why Divergence or Erasure should be unplayable - it'd just change the tone and focus immensely, but I think it'd be extremely interesting to explore those!<br /> Merger and Retreat, on the other hand, don't really seem playable to me currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T11:54:17-08:00","id":1193995,"title":"","content":"Just to avoid giving the wrong impression about my judgement of BPG, I'm going to state I'm absolutely enthusiastic about the vast majority of its content. The book was entirely worth its long, eager wait and more. It is going to be as necessary at the table as the corebook. Things I especially appreciated included acknowledgment the Devouring can resemble the Homecoming at times, guidelines to play various elements of Beast existence (minus the Families stuff since my preferred playstyle tends to deemphasize splat stereotypes), the new Families (especially Tallassii) and Hungers (both equally), most new Atavisms (special mention to Caught in the Webs, Crushing Coils, Enemy Within, Lightning Strike, and Skin Deep, which provide welcome plugs to noticeable gaps in the Beast arsenal), rules for Horrorspawn (they provide an excellent and most useful minion option for the Begotten), the ideas for factions in Beast society (loved the Athenaeum of the Dark Mother and the Incarnate cults), the rules for Beasts to roam the Astral at large, and expansion of the rules for Incarnates (I just regret we get no Ascension-style option for a character to progress beyond Incarnation).<br /> <br /> I also find a few new Nightmares and rules for Cults interesting (even if I tend to focus on Atavisms more) and I fancy the rules for Communion with the Dark Mother (even if I need to check how they apply in practice). I love the Horrorspawn, Legendary Horror (even if I'm dubious it is worth the Satiety price), and Well-Stocked Lair Merits. I would have really liked a Merit to get a second Hunger option, even if Alien Mindset admittedly can work as a stopgap substitute. Obcasus rites are awesome on paper to give Beasts their own magic, even if the given rites examples are nothing to write home about. More or less the same applies for Kinship Merits. Given my own transhumanist mindset, Incarnation is the only Inheritance option I fancy and I'm interested in as a character achievement. There are a few items that look like a waste of space and ink. Doppelganger, Plague Bearer, and Shadow Stalker, I'm looking at you. It is beyond me how anyone may be interested in having them when we have Horrorspawn for minions, Alien Mindset for impersonation, Basilik's Touch for lethal debuffing, and Shadowed Soul for merging with shadows. All in all, BPG .is a top-quality book, I'm already impatient for the PoD option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:12:55-08:00","id":1194002,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love Doppelganger, plague bearer and shadow stalker, as they open many possibilities for social havoc.<br /> They may be more niche, but still definitly have their place as &quot;nightmarish&quot;abilities. And easy to use to cause integrity breaks, which is nice for beasts.<br /> <br /> And the Stepping sideways merit is really awesome, imo.<br /> Feigning Death made me happy. I want more of those, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-10-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:32:34-08:00","id":1194008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194002#post1194002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I love Doppelganger, plague bearer and shadow stalker, as they open many possibilities for social havoc.<br /> They may be more niche, but still definitly have their place as &amp;quot;nightmarish&amp;quot;abilities. And easy to use to cause integrity breaks, which is nice for beasts.<br /> <br /> And the Stepping sideways merit is really awesome, imo.<br /> Feigning Death made me happy. I want more of those, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one that lets you see Twilight was a much-needed addition as well, in my opinion. It opens up a lot of options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:43:34-08:00","id":1194010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193994#post1193994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, not all Beasts want to or have to go for Inheritance (e.g. Predators are mentioned to quite often forego that option, as they often consider their 'normal' status to be the Dark Mother's will, 'pure', and a sort of perfect state/existence).<br /> Also, as you yourself pointed out, Archmages and Elder Vampire PCs became an option once we had Sourcebooks for them - this is not the case for Beasts, currently, but that could very well change at some point (Hell, I'm all for that!). In addition, I don't see why Divergence or Erasure should be unplayable - it'd just change the tone and focus immensely, but I think it'd be extremely interesting to explore those!<br /> Merger and Retreat, on the other hand, don't really seem playable to me currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stated opinion of Predators is another thing in the book I'm rather unhappy with (since I fancy Incarnation a lot and Prey is one of my preferred Hungers) and I'm going to ignore it. It makes little sense to me since I can easily think of all kinds of ways Inheritance can make a Beast an even better predator, and hence I expect many Predators are going to think the Dark Mother made them very good but gave them an option to evolve into something even better. The difference between Incarnates and Archmages or Elder Vampires as PC is the latter two got no real coverage of their nature and abilties that would enable to play them until we got their sourcebooks, whileas everything really necessary to play an Incarnate is included in the corebook already. Having said that, if OPP ever plans to release a sourcebook that is going to expand coverage of Incarnation as a playable high-powered character option (say a Primordial Dream sourcebook), my money is ready and eager to be spent.<br /> <br /> Divergence or Erasure may or may not be playable pretty much the same way one may regard Prometheans and their endgame of becoming a mortal an appealing option to play or not. YMMV, but if I'd want to play a mortal with a few minor special tricks and behind-the-curtain knowledge, I'd make one from scratch. As a rule, I regard pretty much any supernatural splat a better condition to exist in the CoD setting than a mortal, and hence the regressive quest to turn from the former to the latter registers as deeply unrewarding and unappealing to me. This most definitely applies to beasts, since they get high in my 'CoD Isekai' preference list, together with mages, vampires, and sin-eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:03:16-08:00","id":1194033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194010#post1194010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stated opinion of Predators is another thing in the book I'm rather unhappy with (since I fancy Incarnation a lot and Prey is one of my preferred Hungers) and I'm going to ignore it. It makes little sense to me since I can easily think of all kinds of ways Inheritance can make a Beast an even better predator, and hence I expect many Predators are going to think the Dark Mother made them very good but gave them an option to evolve into something even better. The difference between Incarnates and Archmages or Elder Vampires as PC is the latter two got no real coverage of their nature and abilties that would enable to play them until we got their sourcebooks, whileas everything really necessary to play an Incarnate is included in the corebook already. Having said that, if OPP ever plans to release a sourcebook that is going to expand coverage of Incarnation as a playable high-powered character option (say a Primordial Dream sourcebook), my money is ready and eager to be spent.<br /> <br /> Divergence or Erasure may or may not be playable pretty much the same way one may regard Prometheans and their endgame of becoming a mortal an appealing option to play or not. YMMV, but if I'd want to play a mortal with a few minor special tricks and behind-the-curtain knowledge, I'd make one from scratch. As a rule, I regard pretty much any supernatural splat a better condition to exist in the CoD setting than a mortal, and hence the regressive quest to turn from the former to the latter registers as deeply unrewarding and unappealing to me. This most definitely applies to beasts, since they get high in my 'CoD Isekai' preference list, together with mages, vampires, and sin-eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didnt say all Predators Stay away from Inheritance, just that they have a statistical preference. One that to me at least, makes sense.<br /> Imo we lack a lot of Information to make an end-game Incarnate chronicle. The source books for archmages and elder vampires also gave possible adversaries, plot hooks, goals etc. We have little in that way for Incarnates, and I'd love to see more.<br /> <br /> I get that it's your personal preference to go for the highest state possible.To a degree, I even agree. However, I think all the other possibilities are more than justified, and have an intrigue on their own. The stories they can tell have a unique quality.<br /> And Story is the reason why I'd be interested in keeping to play a promethean after achieving the great work: Emotional and narrative investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:07:44-08:00","id":1194035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193989#post1193989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really, <i>really </i>think that fear of rape is something you want to explore through your game, <i>and </i>you have a Storyteller and other players who are willing <i>and </i>comfortable with that, then there's absolutely nothing stopping you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd prefer it if my RPG books didn't include a passage called, &quot;And here's how you play a rape monster!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ask my amoral opinion born from playing a sizable amount of rape hentai eroge (where for the record I tend to find the victim's PoV rather more interesting), I assume fear of rape might turn out to be a not so rewarding option to be (or play) an incarnate nightmare clad in human flesh, if nothing else because its scope tends to feel boring and too narrow after a while. There is only so much variation you can put into violence and sex, and moreso their mandatory combination. It would be more or less the same feeling of &quot;is there anything else to my existence&quot; a different kind of Beast may get after they eviscerate their one hundredth victim. It is what the Begotten invented the Lessons culture to counteract if one puts moral scruples aside. So I'd find the passage you mention a waste of space in most circumstances, if not for the same reasons as you probably do. By the way, this is also the same reason I'd expect many beasts to experiment with variations in their Hunger preferences and hunting M.O. in the long term. I expect repetition boredom to be a significant problem for successful, long-lived beasts, more so than any moral concern they likely outgrew or lacked in the first place.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I just appreciate it a lot when my RPG books or my fellow gamers do not throw all kinds of &quot;badwrongfun&quot; guilt-tripping SJW lectures my way for playing characters whose nature, lifestyle, or abilities may have rapey (or other PC-questionable) implications. As much as I'm concerned, the generic advice to avoid situations that may make other peoples at the table seriously uncomfortable should suffice, I can easily agree with it, and I much prefer if it does not make any 'sacred cow' special status for sexual or any other specific content. More or less the same applies as it concerns other kinds of potentially questionable content, such as slavery or ethnic prejudice. As a rule, I'm not typically going to bring this kind of stuff much further in my typical vanilla RPG than say stating my amoral PC are going to use their mind control abilities for offstage activities that may qualify as supernatural date rape when they feel horny and look for a one-night stand. Anything kinkier than that, I am likely going to leave to sexual RP with the right kind of cooperative partner or my collection of erotic computer games. Of course, if the group is willing to experiment with stronger stuff, I'm certainly not going to be the one to hold back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:29:32-08:00","id":1194041,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you're looking for a safe space where you can act out ideas or fantasies that you know other people are going to find uncomfortable, offensive or disgusting. As I said, if you wish to do so in your games, and can convince the other people at your table to go along with it? Knock yourself out!<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I'd ask you to please leave that stuff out of this discussion and this community. I'm entirely uninterested in hashing out exactly &quot;how much rape is too much&quot; while trying to discuss a series of RPGs that absolutely explore darker themes, but are content to handle such topics with a general maturity and grace that leaves it up to the individual player and group to decide <i>just</i> how far they'd like to take it. And while I don't claim to speak for anyone but myself, I wouldn't be surprised if most others here feel the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:36:12-08:00","id":1194044,"title":"","content":"Anyone think we should make a Homebrew Obascus Rites thread?<br /> <br /> My first idea would be something to actually allow Beasts to do more with Dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:47:29-08:00","id":1194050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194033#post1194033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didnt say all Predators Stay away from Inheritance, just that they have a statistical preference. One that to me at least, makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't to me, but I assume we are going to agree to disagree on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imo we lack a lot of Information to make an end-game Incarnate chronicle. The source books for archmages and elder vampires also gave possible adversaries, plot hooks, goals etc. We have little in that way for Incarnates, and I'd love to see more. </div> </div> </div>We are in full agreement about that. I'd absolutely love to get more information on that kind of stuff for Incarnates, such as in a book about the Primordial Dream or the high-end movers and shakers of beast society. I greedily lapped on the bits about the Begotten luminaries and the factions they created in the BPG, and loved most Incarnate NPC in the book (especially the one said to be the origin for the Bigfoot cryptid myth). Unlike the ones in Conquering Heroes, where the authors seemingly went out of their way to make almost all Inheritance examples hardly usable except as enemy NPC (well, perhaps understandable if one thinks of the book as an adversaries catalogue).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that it's your personal preference to go for the highest state possible.To a degree, I even agree. However, I think all the other possibilities are more than justified, and have an intrigue on their own. The stories they can tell have a unique quality.<br /> And Story is the reason why I'd be interested in keeping to play a promethean after achieving the great work: Emotional and narrative investment. </div> </div> </div>I get your point, and I respect it even if I do not share it. Personally I'm too invested in optimism and self-realization to find most stories with a downer ending rewarding, especially the ones I'm having an active part in developing, such as RPG typically goes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:52:33-08:00","id":1194052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194041#post1194041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, I'd ask you to please leave that stuff out of this discussion and this community. I'm entirely uninterested in hashing out exactly &quot;how much rape is too much&quot; while trying to discuss a series of RPGs that absolutely explore darker themes, but are content to handle such topics with a general maturity and grace that leaves it up to the individual player and group to decide <i>just</i> how far they'd like to take it. And while I don't claim to speak for anyone but myself, I wouldn't be surprised if most others here feel the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine with me. As far as I'm concerned, this tangent branched from my stated displeasure with the Tallassii 'curse', and it begins and ends with that. As a final remark, I'm going to state the curse looks to me as the wrong approach to get what the likes of you seem to want from the game about this topic, and there is little 'maturity and grace' about it. Apart from annoying people like me, it just creates a 'forbidden fruit' dynamic. Better leave the things you want unspoken, unspoken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:58:58-08:00","id":1194055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194044#post1194044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone think we should make a Homebrew Obascus Rites thread?<br /> <br /> My first idea would be something to actually allow Beasts to do more with Dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be a great idea. The Rites look like an excellent idea on paper, and I think most of the community did appreciate the option to give beasts their own kind of 'blood magic', but in practice there is scarcely one rite in the book I'd make my characters bother learning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:03:01-08:00","id":1194056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194055#post1194055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be a great idea. The Rites look like an excellent idea on paper, and I think most of the community did appreciate the option to give beasts their own kind of 'blood magic', but in practice there is scarcely one rite in the book I'd make my characters bother learning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I get that they shouldn't invalidate other types of powers, but having to deal with all the trouble that comes with human sacrifice is not even remotely a trade for a chance at a plot hook or two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:39:12-08:00","id":1194064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194056#post1194056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">all the trouble that comes with human sacrifice</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a ritual that's not supposed to be seen by non-participants in a game where every PC has a personal killing floor, relatively easy access to destructive forces, and no mechanical compulsion against killing outside of fairly specific circumstances. Somehow I get the feeling Beasts don't have a lot of trouble making a murder into a missing persons case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:55:03-08:00","id":1194070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194064#post1194064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a ritual that's not supposed to be seen by non-participants in a game where every PC has a personal killing floor, relatively easy access to destructive forces, and no mechanical compulsion against killing outside of fairly specific circumstances. Somehow I get the feeling Beasts don't have a lot of trouble making a murder into a missing persons case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm largely in agreement, except as it concerns the fact beasts do not have much of an easy option to erase or muddle forensic evidence (short of unleashing the right kind of Lair Traits on the area), or an organized Masquerade to get it buried. So they may still need some caution to avoid turning a murder into a kidnapping case. As an aside, if everything goes wrong, Beast abilities are also great to stage a jailbreak, if the character does not mind living as a fugitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:57:30-08:00","id":1194072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194070#post1194070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm largely in agreement, except as it concerns the fact beasts do not have much of an easy option to erase or muddle forensic evidence (short of unleashing the right kind of Lair Traits on the area), or an organized Masquerade to get it buried. So they may still need some caution to avoid turning a murder into a kidnapping case. As an aside, if everything goes wrong, Beast abilities are also great to stage a jailbreak, if the character does not mind living as a fugitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a pocket dimension where most people keep their soul. That tends to be a fairly secure place to bury the bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:01:45-08:00","id":1194075,"title":"","content":"Organizing my list of existent Nightmares - \u201cYou Don\u2019t Belong Here\u201d is used as an example of a character specific kinship one, but I think it works more generally as a perfect Promethean kinship Nightmare!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:01:55-08:00","id":1194077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194072#post1194072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a pocket dimension where most people keep their soul. That tends to be a fairly secure place to bury the bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of stuff like fingerprints, bloodstains, and DNA evidence, rather than bodies (which I wholly agree with you about). How is a careless beast supposed to deal with them, short of unleashing destructive Lair Traits on the area to wipe them away? One more reason to always have a couple of them in your Lair arsenal, thematic purity be damned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:04:03-08:00","id":1194078,"title":"","content":"Man, Changelings are not going to respond well to Inguma with the Doppleganger Atavism...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:07:31-08:00","id":1194079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194070#post1194070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm largely in agreement, except as it concerns the fact beasts do not have much of an easy option to erase or muddle forensic evidence (short of unleashing the right kind of Lair Traits on the area)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Enemy Within Atavism will help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:16:00-08:00","id":1194082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194070#post1194070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm largely in agreement, except as it concerns the fact beasts do not have much of an easy option to erase or muddle forensic evidence (short of unleashing the right kind of Lair Traits on the area), or an organized Masquerade to get it buried. So they may still need some caution to avoid turning a murder into a kidnapping case. As an aside, if everything goes wrong, Beast abilities are also great to stage a jailbreak, if the character does not mind living as a fugitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Beast would need to be pretty sloppy to leave a strong enough earthly evidence trail for mundane police to link a disappearance to their mortal identity.<br /> <br /> Now, enough evidence for a competent in-the-know Hunter Conspiracy to make the connection - that\u2019s another story... hook... entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T23:59:25-08:00","id":1194156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194044#post1194044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone think we should make a Homebrew Obascus Rites thread?<br /> <br /> My first idea would be something to actually allow Beasts to do more with Dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this as well. Shall I make the thread? I've got an idea for a first Rite, one that interacts with a Temple to make it easier for all Beasts involved in the performance of the Rite to open Pathways to and from the Temple, as well as protecting it from damage due to Lair Traits. Does that sound like an Intermediate Rite or an Advanced one to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:15:36-07:00","id":1194248,"title":"","content":"Id say basic or even intermediate. And please do","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:21:16-07:00","id":1194250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194248#post1194248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id say basic or even intermediate. And please do</div> </div> </div> </div>I have made it now, here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1194163-homebrew-obcasus-rites\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-obcasus-rites</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:42:17-07:00","id":1194262,"title":"","content":"Just started reading the Atavisms. Alien mindset is cool! That Satiety Expenditure would be neat trick for ensuring your hunger is fulfilled but you don't drive it all the way to 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:15:43-07:00","id":1194280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1192772#post1192772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship merits are an awesome idea! Its neat to have a way to pick of some of the characteristics of other splats if you are trying to emulate a specific type of monster. Scour Your Body is a particularly interesting and non-obvious one for Mage.<br /> <br /> Legendary Horror is also AWESOME! Ways to get access to Influences are always fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legendary Horror and Horrorspawn certainly bring awesome benefits (although you only get access to Influences and Numina in your Lair), but they carry a serious Satiety bill, esp. if you have both of them, use a lot of Essence, and/or keep your Horrorspawn minions around a lot of time. You are going to work your ass off hunting or using Family Dinner if you have these Merits. Legendary Horror is doubly useful for Incarnates since they are merged with their Horror and hence can tap spirit powers all the time.<br /> <br /> Well-Stocked Lair is another nice Merit to have, in order to draw extra usefulness from your Lair as a hideout.<br /> <br /> Kinship Merits are an awesome idea in theory, but just like kinship Nightmares, in practice the usefulness of specific Merits may vary significantly. Ghost (Look Between Worlds, Walk Lightly), Werewolf (Scent Your Prey, Step Sideways), and Mage (Scour Your Body) Kinship Merits seem rather good to have, Vampire Kinship (Feign Death, Sanguivore) ones not so much. I'd assume 'ghost' kinship actually refers to sin-eaters in most cases. Usefulness of Know Their Falseness may vary considerably depending on how much deal-making the Beast does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-11-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:35:45-07:00","id":1194294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194280#post1194280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship Merits are an awesome idea in theory, but just like kinship Nightmares, in practice the usefulness of specific Merits may vary significantly. Changeling, Ghost, Werewolf, and Mage Kinship Merits seem rather good to have, Vampire Kinship ones not so much. I'd assume 'ghost' kinship actually refers to sin-eaters in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very certain that ghost was intentional since they are the most pop culture of the three ephemeral entities that are in every single 2e corebook (expect Requiem).<br /> <br /> As for the usefulness, chronicles are scenario dependent as it is. Trying to whiteroom merits doesn't work since you need context. Feign Death could be useful for evading enemy combatants, avoiding airborne toxins, or travelling underwater for extended periods. There are lots of creative things you could do with not needing to breathe. Sanguivore gives you an extra weapon that can't be disarmed and is much more subtle than most Atavisms. If you're playing a game with vampire politics, you could use it to frame vampire for breaching the masquerade, then avoid suspicion if the Kindred know you're not a vampire. Or alternatively, you could use both merits together to reinforce your Passing Resemblance as a vampire. Instead of just appearing not to breathe, Feign Death lets you actually not breathe. I can see scenarios where those little details could be lifesavers.<br /> <br /> Actually, that idea of using kinship merits to reinforce passing resemblance is interesting. I'm going to think on that some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-11-2018, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T09:11:06-07:00","id":1194862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1193989#post1193989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd prefer it if my RPG books didn't include a passage called, &quot;And here's how you play a rape monster!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read all of it yet - in as far as I have the curse has had relatively little airtime in favour of imprisonment imagery. But is there really a passage called that?<br /> <br /> My own problem with Family from I've read so far is that it seems more like a Hunger - kidnapping and imprisoning people <i>could</i> come under any of Power, Hoard, Prey, or Punishment, but with that many others it could be, I'd say it's powerful enough to be its own. But that's what it seems like - an action rather than a nature, and a Hunger rather than a Family. A Family seems more like it should reflect other forms of entrapment: not just imprisonment, but stifling claustrophobia, or being lost underground, or buried alive.<br /> <br /> I like the Inguma, though. And the two new Hungers are excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T09:20:30-07:00","id":1194866,"title":"","content":"I'm back, reading the BPG and, just as I charged some cash for the PDF way before it arrived, I'm gonna do the same for the Print-On-Demand later this evening.<br /> <br /> I don't think I have something to say that would be significantly different from what has been said already nor do i think that my detailed opinion would be that interesting to read, but the book's great and gives us all more room to breathe, more canon to explore and brand new material to use. It is no more than what I expected, but that's just because I expected <i>a lot</i> (and was not disappointed in the slightest).<br /> <br /> Kudos to all those involved. This is shaping up to become one of my favorite supplements ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:59:40-07:00","id":1194896,"title":"","content":"Is the 'curse' on Talassi actually defined anywhere? I don't see it in the Family's writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T11:08:15-07:00","id":1194903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194862#post1194862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read all of it yet - in as far as I have the curse has had relatively little airtime in favour of imprisonment imagery. But is there really a passage called that?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there isn't. Gellydog was saying that it would have been distasteful to include such a passage in response to another user disliking that Tasallii downplayed the rape angle instead of playing it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:37:05-07:00","id":1194934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194896#post1194896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the 'curse' on Talassi actually defined anywhere? I don't see it in the Family's writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be. It's in the first few paragraphs of the write-up.<br /> <br /> ...although that's about it. There are no game mechanics attached to that aspect of the Talassi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:45:06-07:00","id":1194937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1192676-beast-player-s-guide-on-dtrpg?p=1194934#post1194934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be. It's in the first few paragraphs of the write-up.<br /> ...although that's about it. There are no game mechanics attached to that aspect of the Talassi.</div> </div> </div> </div>...is 'the curse' just the fact that they're branded as kidnappers or rapists? I figured that was just kind of something that naturally followed from their nature/likely abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:54:59-07:00","id":1194942,"title":"","content":"aaaaand I got the Player Guide. Can't wait to find time and delve into it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"